{
  "_comment": "SYNTHETIC, not a capture. Every bounds.center here is a PART-LOCAL authored value,\nwhich is what Part.boundsCentroidOffset is and what the mod puts on the wire today.\nThe real captures beside this file predate that: they carry the old fork's\nvessel-frame mesh centroid under the same field name, so none of them can exercise\nthe frame conversion in buildShipMapPart.\n\nThe two RV-105 blocks are the clearest case: one authored offset (0, 0.34, 0) serving\nboth instances, because boundsCentroidOffset is per PART. Added raw it runs up the\nspine for both and leaves them sunk in the hull; rotated by each mount it pushes them\nout to their own sides. The four radial decouplers carry a smaller, physically\nplausible 0.12 m offset. The two tilted panels carry an offset perpendicular to their\nown up, the case where the roll about up is not on the wire and only the offset's\nlength and its up-aligned component stay exact.",
